    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0249" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/524</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Iranian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schayesteh</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 501</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-03">June 3, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Minister of Iran presents his compliments to His Excellency the Secretary of
                    State and has the honor to bring to his attention the following:</p>
                <p>The Iranian Government desires to engage in this country an American financial
                    expert in Government Finance. He should have a broad knowledge and experience in
                    the financial field.</p>
                <p>The Minister of Iran would appreciate it very much if the Honorable the Secretary
                    of State would find and suggest a suitable candidate for this position.</p>
            </div>
